# Shell wait

Start a long repository command with `block_until_ms: 0`. Continue other work. The completion notice is the end signal.

Poll with AwaitShell only when the next step is blocked on that process. Wait for process exit. A pattern is valid only when that line cannot appear before the command ends.

Require process exit and the Check Evidence Line when `make check` or `make check-full` is requested. A printed step success, including transaction-control verification, is not the result of the run.

`Error:` is not an AwaitShell pattern. It is an expected Storage Activation reject (`MissingOrInactive` / `IdentityMismatch`).

Set the poll window from the command class:

| Command | Typical duration |
|---|---|
| GitHub PR `verify` check | about 2 minutes |
| `make check-fast` | about 1 minute after a build |
| Clean `make check` | about 10 minutes |
| Clean `make check-full` | about 20 minutes |

The Check Evidence Line is the last line of each tier, so it is a valid end pattern.
